<title>USA: USDA consolidates APHIS field offices.</title>
<headline>USDA consolidates APHIS field offices.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Monday said the Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service (APHIS) would consolidate its 13 field offices into two regional hubs.</p>
<p>USDA said about 150 employees would be relocated to a hub in Raleigh, N.C. and about 160 employees would be relocated to a hub in Ft. Collins, Colo.</p>
<p>USDA said the university communities in both cities would offer APHIS employees &quot;substantial training opportunities and contribute to the diversity of the workforce.&quot;</p>
